# Cursor rules — see CLAUDE.md for the full guide.

This project's full AI guide is in CLAUDE.md at the repo root. Read it
before suggesting changes. Architectural decisions live in plan.md.

Quick reminders for Cursor:

- TypeScript strict mode is enforced (`strict`, `noUncheckedIndexedAccess`,
  `exactOptionalPropertyTypes`, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`).
  Never weaken these. Prefer narrowing over `as` / `any`.
- New features go in `api/src/modules/<feature>/` with controller, service,
  model, DTOs.
- Validation at the boundary via `class-validator` DTOs and the global
  `ValidationPipe` (whitelist + forbidNonWhitelisted + transform).
- Authorization is a service/guard concern. Owner-scoped reads filter by
  `user_id` in the service query, never in the controller.
- Errors via `HttpException`; the global exception filter shapes the
  response. No `res.status(...).json(...)`.
- No `console.log` in production code; use the Nest `Logger`. Delete dead
  code rather than commenting it out.
- Multi-row state changes go inside a Sequelize transaction. The
  application-approval cascade is the canonical example.
- Commits never include AI co-author trailers. Author is
  `Riquelmy Melara <riquelmy.melara@tecniastudio.com>`.

See CLAUDE.md for layout, commands, and the "do not touch" list.
